\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces Examples of multi-view data.\relax }}{2}{figure.caption.8}
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.2}{\ignorespaces An example to demonstrate the advantages of having multiple views. As the number of views increases, each view adds new complementary information. The learning algorithm leverages this information to improve its performance on each test data sample.\relax }}{3}{figure.caption.9}
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.3}{\ignorespaces Batch methods vs. Incremental methods: (a) Batch methods have to retrain on all the historical data after every addition. (b) Incremental methods only need the old model and new data samples to update the model after every addition.\relax }}{6}{figure.caption.11}
